 ('Deleting', 'PermanentDeletion', 'DeleteFolderTree', 'shutil.rmtree(path)', 'shutil.rmtree deletes a folder with everything in it, irreversibly; it raises FileNotFoundError for a missing path, unless ignore_errors=True.', ("(lambda g: (exec('import os, shutil, tempfile, zipfile, io\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nt = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())\\n(t/\\'spam\\'/\\'eggs\\').mkdir(parents=True)\\n(t/\\'spam\\'/\\'eggs\\'/\\'f.txt\\').write_text(\\'x\\')\\nshutil.rmtree(t/\\'spam\\')\\nshutil.rmtree(t/\\'spam\\', ignore_errors=True)\\ntry:\\n    shutil.rmtree(t/\\'spam\\')\\n    second = \\'no error\\'\\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\\n    second = \\'FileNotFoundError\\'\\nout = ((t/\\'spam\\').exists(), second)\\nshutil.rmtree(t)\\n', g), g['out'])[1])({})", "(False, 'FileNotFoundError')")),
 ('Deleting', 'PermanentDeletion', 'DeletionErrors', 'shutil.rmtree(path, onexc=handler)', 'Instead of stopping, rmtree can call a handler with the failing function, the path and the exception; the onexc parameter exists since Python 3.12 and replaces the deprecated onerror, whose handler receives an exception-information tuple instead of the exception.', ("(lambda g: (exec('import os, shutil, tempfile, zipfile, io\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nt = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())\\nseen = []\\nshutil.rmtree(t/\\'missing\\', onexc=lambda func, path, exc: seen.append((Path(path).name, type(exc).__name__)))\\nout = seen\\nshutil.rmtree(t)\\n', g), g['out'])[1])({})", "[('missing', 'FileNotFoundError')]")),
 ('Deleting', 'SaferDeletion', 'DryRun', "print('Deleting', filename)  # os.unlink(filename)", "A dry run replaces the dangerous call with a print, so the program shows what it would delete, copy, rename or move before it does so; the chapter's typo *.rxt for *.txt is found this way.", ("(lambda g: exec('import os, shutil, tempfile, zipfile, io\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nt = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())\\n(t/\\'a.txt\\').write_text(\\'x\\')\\n(t/\\'b.txt\\').write_text(\\'y\\')\\nfor i in range(n):\\n    (t/(\\'extra%d.txt\\' % i)).write_text(\\'x\\')\\nwould = [f.name for f in sorted(t.glob(\\'*.rxt\\'))]\\nwould_fixed = [f.name for f in sorted(t.glob(\\'*.txt\\'))]\\nout = (would, would_fixed, sorted(p.name for p in t.iterdir()))\\nshutil.rmtree(t)\\n', g) or g['out'])({'n': 0})", "([], ['a.txt', 'b.txt'], ['a.txt', 'b.txt'])")),
